In classic WoW, most warlocks used Voidwalkers because they were **summonable pets** (unlike Succubus, which required a talent and was not a pet). Voidwalkers provided **threat generation** (via Torment/Suffering) and **utility** (Sacrifice for survivability), making them essential for dungeons and raids where pets were mandatory. The Succubus, while stronger in damage (Lash of Pain) and CC (Seduction), was **not a pet** and thus couldn’t be used in many group activities. [end of text]


